      <activity id="3b752290-7b1a-5330-bb7e-2a821a09db16" activityNameId="52eed060-9841-5ce8-baeb-1db7bfdc7e11" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, desktop computer, to WEEE treatment</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, desktop computer, to WEEE treatment
mix process of the two disposal ways - the manual dismantling and the mechanical treatment (in a shredder). Update 2023: The average mass of 8.8 kg is used as in the dataset for desktop computer, where the split to manual and mechanical treatment is assumed to be the same as in the original dataset. Another change is that the batteries flows are now removed since desktop computers do not contain lithium ion batteries.; Geography: data of the situation in Switzerland; UUID: 9d4409e7-2033-437d-9caf-dee8ac2f63b9
This dataset represents the statistical mixture of the two different disposal ways for WEEE devices in Switzerland.
Location: data of the situation in Switzerland
Technology: current mix of manual and mechanical treatment in Switzerland
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 82.5 kt total WEEE
Sampling: statistical data
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9d4409e7-2033-437d-9caf-dee8ac2f63b9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
